# 9. INTERACTIVE ENVIRONMENT

The environment should respond to user interaction.

Make selected environmental elements clickable.

Examples:
- Clicking a computer shows the assigned character and their current task.
- Clicking a coffee machine displays a small contextual interaction.
- Clicking a meeting table reveals ongoing or upcoming meetings.
- Clicking a task board opens a compact task overview.
- Clicking a plant may trigger a tiny playful animation.
- Clicking a window may display a short environmental message.
