# 11. NOTIFICATION SYSTEM

Create a fully functional local notification system.

## 11.1. Completion Notifications

When a character completes a task:
- Display a small toast notification.
- Include the character's portrait.
- Include the character's name.
- Show the completed task title.
- Display a short, friendly message.
- Include a subtle visual animation.
- Optionally play a soft notification sound.

Example messages:
- "Mochi finished organizing the research notes!"
- "Pip completed a design review!"
- "Bean wrapped up the latest coding task!"
- "Luna finished preparing the meeting notes!"

Vary the messages naturally.

Avoid loud, disruptive, or excessively frequent notifications.

## 11.2. Notification Center

Provide a notification panel accessible from the header.

It should display recent events, including task completions.

Allow users to:
- Open the notification center.
- Dismiss individual notifications.
- Clear all notifications.
- Mark notifications as read.
- See a badge for unread notifications.

## 11.3. Notification Settings

Provide a notification enable/disable toggle.

When notifications are disabled:
- Do not display completion toasts.
- Do not play notification sounds.
- Continue updating task progress normally.
- Continue recording activity in the activity log.
- Preserve the user's setting during the current browser session.

Distinguish notification sounds from ambient background music.

Turning off notifications must not automatically stop the background music.

Persist the notification preference locally.

